{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>To us and to our kindred.</b> To our families. And its midrash: even the wood of our cradles he revealed to us." "<b>And we have a father and a brother.</b> — that we have a father and a brother." "<b>According to these words.</b> According to his questions that he asked — we were compelled to tell." "<b>If he will say.</b> Which he will say — for כִּי serves in the sense of אִם, and אִם serves in the sense of אֲשֶׁר; this is one of the four usages in which כִּי serves, namely אִם — for this כִּי is like אִם, as in ״עַד אִם דִּבַּרְתִּי דְּבָרָי״ (Genesis 24:33)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:19.138089443Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}